      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Court of Appeal in *Thorne v. Maritime Logistics Ltd* (2023) dismissed the appeal, holding that the doctrine of vicarious proximity from *Duncombe v. Northern Rail* (2014) does not extend to sub-contracted employees where the control test in *Smith v. Jones* (2018) is satisfied. The court relied on *Henderson v. Global Shipping* (2020) to determine that high autonomy precludes vicarious liability, while reaffirming *Miller v. Transport Corp* (2019) that proximity must be both physical and legal. Ultimately, the judgment clarifies that modern logistics decouple direct supervision from operational responsibility, limiting the duty of care to those with direct control.",
